Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: Break the themed taskbar repaint loop in CTaskSwitchWnd.
 OnEraseBackground invalidated the TBSTYLE_TRANSPARENT task toolbar on
 every erase; with an active msstyles theme the builtin comctl32 toolbar
 forwards WM_ERASEBKGND to its parent on every WM_PAINT, so the invalidate
 re-triggered the paint and closed an infinite repaint loop (100% CPU,
 message queue never drained, WM_TIMER starvation froze the taskbar bridge
 sync and the tray clock). Drop the InvalidateRect; the toolbar repaints
 itself on its own invalidations and layout/theme changes go through
 OnSize/UpdateButtonsSize.
Last-Modified: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:34:45 +0300

--- a/src/base/shell/explorer/taskswnd.cpp
+++ b/src/base/shell/explorer/taskswnd.cpp
@@ -2354,7 +2354,14 @@
         {
             DrawThemeParentBackground(m_hWnd, hdc, &rect);
         }
-        m_TaskBar.InvalidateRect(NULL, FALSE);
+
+        /* Do NOT invalidate the task toolbar here. The toolbar is created
+           with TBSTYLE_TRANSPARENT, so the builtin comctl32 toolbar forwards
+           WM_ERASEBKGND to us on every WM_PAINT; invalidating it from this
+           handler re-triggers its paint and closes an infinite repaint loop
+           (100% CPU, message queue never drains, WM_TIMER starvation).
+           The toolbar still repaints itself on its own invalidations, and
+           layout/theme changes go through OnSize/UpdateButtonsSize. */
 
         return TRUE;
     }
